          "bbox": [
            0.689,
            0.048,
            0.861,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Fractions in Disguise"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.088,
            0.651,
            0.11
          ],
          "content": "The percentage target achieved is visualised below."
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "bbox": [
            0.228,
            0.123,
            0.472,
            0.227
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_chart_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.277,
            0.227,
            0.41,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{2000}{5000} \\times 100 = 40\\%",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "bbox": [
            0.527,
            0.123,
            0.77,
            0.227
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.576,
                0.227,
                0.708,
                0.251
              ],
              "content": "3500 5000 × 100 = 70%"
            }
          ],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_chart_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.279,
            0.249,
            0.425,
            0.276
          ],
          "content": "40\\% = \\frac{40}{100} = \\frac{2}{5} = 0.4",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.577,
            0.249,
            0.731,
            0.276
          ],
          "content": "70\\% = \\frac{70}{100} = \\frac{7}{10} = 0.7",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.282,
            0.511,
            0.302
          ],
          "content": "It is 40% on Day 1 and 70% on Day 2."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.301,
            0.845,
            0.34
          ],
          "content": "Another way of saying it is — he was 60% short of his target on Day 1 and 30% short of his target on Day 2."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.341,
            0.846,
            0.382
          ],
          "content": "? In the next two days, he made ₹5000 and ₹6000 respectively. What percentage of his target are these values?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.384,
            0.846,
            0.423
          ],
          "content": "His target is ₹5000, and he made ₹5000 on Day 3 — this is 100%. On Day 4, he made ₹6000, which is 1000 more than his target."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.423,
            0.683,
            0.449
          ],
          "content": "? What percentage of the target was achieved on Day 4?"
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.459,
            0.489,
            0.556
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_chart_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.25,
            0.555,
            0.395,
            0.58
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{5000}{5000} \\times 100 = 100\\%",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_15.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.523,
            0.459,
            0.793,
            0.556
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_image_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.57,
            0.555,
            0.715,
            0.58
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{6000}{5000} \\times 100 = 120\\%",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_17.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.247,
            0.578,
            0.4,
            0.604
          ],
          "content": "100\\% = \\frac{100}{100} = \\frac{1}{1} = 1.0",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.566,
            0.578,
            0.719,
            0.604
          ],
          "content": "120\\% = \\frac{120}{100} = \\frac{6}{5} = 1.2",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_19.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.61,
            0.846,
            0.675
          ],
          "content": "1000 is 20% of 5000. Therefore, 6000, (5000 + 1000) is $100\\% + 20\\%$ = 120% of 5000. It can also be computed as $\\frac{6000}{5000} \\times 100 = \\frac{6}{5} \\times 100 = 120\\%.$ This means he achieved 120% of his target, i.e., 20% more than his target."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.676,
            0.846,
            0.718
          ],
          "content": "？ On Days 5 and 6 his sales were ₹7800 and ₹9550 respectively. Calculate the percentage of the target achieved on these days."
        },
        {
